wbanish (0.4.0-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * GNOME: keep working after the screen locks, and when GNOME switches the
    extension off and on again; wbanish waits for it instead of exiting.
  * GNOME: a click or scroll while the cursor is hidden shows it again and
    reaches the window, which keeps the pointer while the cursor is hidden.
  * GNOME: support GNOME 42 to 45, explain why the extension isn't running,
    and install the extension when wbanish was built without the package.
  * GNOME: -t counts only mouse activity, also during video playback.
  * GNOME: Alt+Shift and other layout switching don't hide the cursor.
  * Don't hide the cursor again for a held key's autorepeat.
  * sway 1.10+: nudge the pointer so that the overlay gets pointer focus.
  * Overlay: remove it when a clicked button is released, not pressed.
  * Don't exit on a Wayland read that dispatches nothing.
  * Refuse X11 sessions, and take --help and --version.
  * Don't start at login on sway, Hyprland and niri, which have this built in.

 -- Komiljon Sobitov <komiljon.sobitov.uzb@gmail.com>  Tue, 20 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0500

